      {"t":"mc","q":"the problems =","o":["i problemi","le probleme","le problemi","i problema"],"why":"problema is masculine, so its plural is i problemi."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"the cities =","o":["le città","le cittàs","le citte","la città"],"why":"Nouns ending in an accented vowel do not change; only the article does: le città."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"i figli can mean…","o":["the children, sons and daughters","only the daughters","only one son","the relatives"],"why":"A mixed group takes the masculine plural, so i figli covers sons and daughters."},
      {"t":"order","p":"the hands","a":["le","mani"],"x":["i"],"why":"mano is feminine, so the plural article is le: le mani."},
      {"t":"order","p":"the brothers","a":["i","fratelli"],"x":["le"],"why":"fratelli is a masculine plural noun, so the article is i."},
      {"t":"order","p":"the photos","a":["le","foto"],"x":["fotos"],"why":"foto is a short form, so it does not change for more than one: le foto."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"__ problema","p":"the problem","a":["il"],"o":["la","i","le"],"why":"problema ends in -a but is masculine: il problema."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"le sorell__","p":"the sisters","a":["e"],"o":["a","i","o"],"why":"Feminine -a becomes -e in the plural: le sorelle."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"i padr__","p":"the fathers","a":["i"],"o":["e","a","o"],"why":"For nouns in -e, the -e becomes -i in the plural, whatever their gender: i padri."},
      {"t":"type","p":"the sisters","a":["le sorelle"],"hint":"sorella","x":["i"],"why":"sorelle is a feminine plural noun, so the article is le."},
      {"t":"type","p":"the hand","a":["la mano"],"hint":"mano · watch the gender","x":["il"],"why":"mano ends in -o but is feminine: la mano."},
      {"t":"type","p":"the grandparents","a":["i nonni"],"hint":"nonno · a mixed group","x":["le"],"why":"A mixed group takes the masculine plural: i nonni."}
